---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Methods — VIOT Research" description="VIOT-3 and VIOT-4 framework architecture.">
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="kicker">Methodology</p>
    <h1>Framework Architecture</h1>
    <div class="prose" style="margin-top:1.5rem;">
      <p>The Virtual Ion-Optics Testbed progressed through four phases. Production results are driven by VIOT-3 (Axisymmetric) and VIOT-4 (3D + DSMC).</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-section border-top">
    <h2>Phase III: VIOT-3 (Axisymmetric)</h2>
    <div class="grid-2">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>VIOT-3 is the production framework for the core erosion campaign. It models barrel erosion (axisymmetric, inside aperture wall).</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Poisson Solver:</strong> SuperLU direct factorization — replaces non-convergent Red-Black SOR from VIOT-2.</li>
          <li><strong>Plasma Push:</strong> True leapfrog with backward half-kick for stable E-field integration.</li>
          <li><strong>Sputter Yield:</strong> 2D (Energy, θ) bilinear interpolation capturing geometric shadowing.</li>
          <li><strong>MCC:</strong> Correct null-collision ratio — fixes ν ∝ ν²Δt² error.</li>
          <li><strong>Injection:</strong> Bohm drift at injection with thermal spread.</li>
          <li><strong>Boundary:</strong> φ = V_screen upstream; plasma cells only for seeding.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>15 Defects Corrected from VIOT-2</h3>
        <p class="text-small" style="margin-bottom:1rem;">The ten most critical (full list in manuscript Table 4):</p>
        <div class="table-wrap">
          <table>
            <thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Defect</th><th>Correction</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="mono">1</td><td>CUDA Red-Black SOR block-sync errors</td><td>SuperLU direct factorization</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="mono">2</td><td>Sputter-yield discarded angle axis</td><td>2D (E, θ) bilinear interpolation</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="mono">3</td><td>Post-CEX velocity set to exactly 0</td><td>Maxwellian sampling at 400 K</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="mono">4</td><td>Half-acceleration push</td><td>True leapfrog + backward half-kick</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="mono">5</td><td>MCC double-counting</td><td>Correct null-collision ratio</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="mono">6</td><td>ν_max at wrong n_gas</td><td>Recomputed from cross-section</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="mono">7</td><td>Erosion ignored macroparticle weight</td><td>Y × w_real</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="mono">8</td><td>Particles seeded inside solid cells</td><td>Plasma cells only</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="mono">9</td><td>Upstream boundary φ=0</td><td>φ = V_screen</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="mono">10</td><td>No Bohm drift at injection</td><td>u_B + thermal spread</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-section border-top">
    <h2>Phase IV: VIOT-4 (3D + DSMC)</h2>
    <div class="grid-2">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>VIOT-4 extends the framework to 3D to capture pit-and-groove erosion on the downstream face and interstitial web.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>DSMC Collision:</strong> No-Time-Counter (NTC) acceptance P = σ·g·dt/V_cell.</li>
          <li><strong>Poisson Operator:</strong> Corrected Laplacian assembly (interior diag +6, off-diagonals -1, residual 1.7e-11).</li>
          <li><strong>MD Pipeline:</strong> LAMMPS AIREBO crystalline MD for graphene substrate interactions.</li>
          <li><strong>3D Mesh:</strong> Hexahedral grid with proper aperture geometry.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Adversarial Review: 5 Bugs Found</h3>
        <ol>
          <li><strong>Poisson operator sign bug</strong> — x/y off-diagonals were +1, z were -1, assembling 6I + Nx + Ny - Nz, not a Laplacian. Fixed: all six off-diagonals -1.</li>
          <li><strong>MD projectile velocity off by 10¹⁰</strong> — unit conversion applied ×1e-12 instead of ×1e-2. Fixed; verified 300 eV Xe → 210 Å/ps.</li>
          <li><strong>Sputter count counted Xe as C</strong> — used total-atom delta. Fixed: count type-1 (C) atoms only.</li>
          <li><strong>Engine reinject teleported all particles</strong> — reseeded every slot each step. Fixed: refill only inactive slots.</li>
          <li><strong>DSMC collision not NTC</strong> — fixed p=0.3 with unused σ. Fixed: proper No-Time-Counter acceptance.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-section border-top">
    <h2>VIOT-2 → VIOT-3 Impact Summary</h2>
    <div class="callout" style="border-radius:12px; padding:2rem;">
      <p class="kicker">Without these corrections</p>
      <p style="margin-bottom:0;">All prior fields unreliable (#1), H3 could not manifest (#2), off-axis erosion underestimated (#3), E-field effectively halved (#4), 10× oversampling (#6), legacy erosion meaningless (#7).</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
